geometry_reference
assembly_id
parameter_set
status
created_revision
modified_revision
deleted_revision
The geometry itself should not necessarily be embedded directly into the primary relational record.

12. GEOMETRY STORAGE
Geometry should be represented through a geometry abstraction layer.
Possible storage approaches include:
serialized geometry
binary geometry references
mesh references
kernel-native representations
2D drawing representations
The relational database stores the identity and relationship.
Object storage can store large generated geometry artifacts where appropriate.

