31. CODE SERVICE — MVP
The first implementation should not attempt to encode every building code in existence.
Instead, the service should establish the architecture for jurisdiction-specific rule sets.
The workflow is:
Project Address
↓
Jurisdiction Resolver
↓
Applicable Regulatory Sources
↓
Source Version
↓
Code Manifest
↓
Rule Dataset
↓
Validation
The architecture must support adding jurisdictions later without redesigning the core project model.

