58. FIRST BUILD TARGET
The first actual development milestone should not be the complete architectural drawing package.
It should be:
PROJECT CREATION → MODEL → SIMPLE BUILDING → DRAWING
A user creates:
2-storey residence
The system creates:
Site
Ground Level
Upper Level
Walls
Doors
Windows
Rooms
Floor slabs
Roof
The system then generates:
Ground Floor Plan
Upper Floor Plan
Four Elevations
One Section
and produces:
ARCH D PDF
If that works from a structured project model, the foundation is proven.

59. SECOND BUILD TARGET
Then implement:
Natural-language modification
Example:
“Move the rear bedroom wall 300 mm north and enlarge the bedroom while keeping the exterior envelope unchanged.”
Aria generates a model command.
The model changes.
Dependencies update.
Affected drawings regenerate.
The customer sees the revision.
That proves that CAD-AI is actually model-aware.

60. THIRD BUILD TARGET
Then implement:
Redline
Customer marks:
“Add another window here.”
Aria interprets the redline.
The system creates the window.
The elevation updates.
The floor plan updates.
The window schedule updates.
The section updates if affected.
This demonstrates the defining OneDraft capability:
one model → coordinated documentation.

61. FOURTH BUILD TARGET
Introduce the first jurisdictional Code Manifest workflow.
The system determines:
Where is the project?
Which regulatory framework applies?
Which versions are applicable?
What rules affect this project?
The system records the resulting manifest before design generation.
The compliance engine then evaluates the project against the configured rules.

62. FIFTH BUILD TARGET
Introduce:
Customer acceptance
The customer receives the complete document package.
The system records:
Project Revision
Model Version
Drawing Set
Validation State
Code Manifest
Redline State
Document Hashes
Acceptance Event
The MVP now has a complete commercial transaction lifecycle.

