No shortcut should bypass the Project Model.
That is the architectural rule that protects OneDraft from becoming an AI image-generation application with CAD-like decoration.

64. VERSION 0.1 DECISION
The OneDraft MVP technical foundation is therefore established as:
Frontend: React / Next.js
Backend: Python / FastAPI
Primary Database: PostgreSQL
Object Storage: S3-compatible
Queue: Redis-backed asynchronous jobs
Deployment: Docker/containerized
AI: Provider-agnostic Aria integration layer
Geometry: Semantic OneDraft model + geometry abstraction + computational geometry kernel
Documentation: Model-derived vector drawing pipeline
Output: ARCH D PDF initially, followed by CAD/BIM interoperability
Architecture: Modular monorepo initially, independently scalable services/workers
Persistence: Versioned Project Model + event/audit history
Core Principle: Project Model remains the single source of truth.

65. ENGINEERING DEFINITION
At this point OneDraft has progressed through four architectural levels:
LEVEL 1 — PRODUCT CONCEPT
CAD-AI — Aria Powered.
LEVEL 2 — PROJECT DATA MODEL
The building becomes a persistent structured computational model.
LEVEL 3 — SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE
AI, model, geometry, compliance, validation and documentation become independent coordinated subsystems.
LEVEL 4 — MVP ENGINEERING ARCHITECTURE
The subsystems now have defined technology boundaries, repositories, APIs, persistence, workers and deployment topology.
The next stage is therefore no longer conceptual.
It is the definition of the actual OneDraft domain schema and API contract.
That stage will specify the concrete objects and operations that the software developers—or a future automated coding system—will implement.
Version 0.1 — MVP Technical Stack & Repository Architecture established.
